Change: run a key bind by name, and the SDK's own F3 / F4 / F7 / backtick binds start unbound

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0017-tools-menu-binds.patch
Status:     port-specific (a small API addition could go upstream)

WHAT
  The port gathers every tool that used to sit on a function key (the SDK's
  debug overlay F3, settings F4, achievements F7, log console `, and the
  port's own F2-F12) into ONE Tools menu on F1, so a stray press of an F key
  no longer opens or switches something mid-game. F11 = fullscreen.

WHY A PATCH
  The menu has to run the SDK's own binds, whose callbacks touch ReXApp's
  private overlay members: only the bind registry can reach them.

CHANGE
  * keybinds.h / .cpp: InvokeBind(name) runs a registered bind's callback as
    if its key had been pressed (callback copied out under the lock first:
    a callback may register binds itself).
  * rex_app.cpp: bind_debug_overlay / bind_console / bind_settings /
    bind_achievements are registered with NO default key. They stay ordinary
    "Keybinds" settings: a key can still be given to any of them by hand
    (settings.toml, e.g. bind_settings = "F4").

diff --git a/include/rex/ui/keybinds.h b/include/rex/ui/keybinds.h
index 3120f16..64cc770 100644
--- a/include/rex/ui/keybinds.h
+++ b/include/rex/ui/keybinds.h
@@ -82,4 +82,13 @@ void UnregisterBind(std::string_view name);
  */
 bool ProcessKeyEvent(KeyEvent& e);
 
+/**
+ * Run a registered bind's callback by name, as if its key was pressed
+ * (for menus that list the binds, e.g. a game's tools menu). Call it on the
+ * thread key events arrive on (the UI thread).
+ * @param name  The CVAR name used when registering the bind.
+ * @return      True if the bind exists and has a callback.
+ */
+bool InvokeBind(std::string_view name);
+
 }  // namespace rex::ui
diff --git a/src/ui/keybinds.cpp b/src/ui/keybinds.cpp
index 9822f3b..b0be86a 100644
--- a/src/ui/keybinds.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/keybinds.cpp
@@ -223,4 +223,23 @@ bool ProcessKeyEvent(KeyEvent& e) {
   return false;
 }
 
+bool InvokeBind(std::string_view name) {
+  /* Copy the callback out first: it may register or unregister binds itself
+     (the lock isn't recursive). */
+  std::function<void()> callback;
+  {
+    std::lock_guard lock(g_binds_mutex);
+    for (auto& entry : g_binds) {
+      if (entry.name == name && entry.callback) {
+        callback = entry.callback;
+        break;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+  if (!callback)
+    return false;
+  callback();
+  return true;
+}
+
 }  // namespace rex::ui
